_start_notice() {
	cat <<'EOF'
The GTK theme follows the QtCurve settings through a watch process. The
process starts at each login. To start it now, run:
systemctl --user start qtcurve-gtk-writer.service

The Firefox chrome and the scroll bars of web pages follow the QtCurve
settings through a second watch process that starts at each login. The
process reads "Apply the settings to Firefox" in the QtCurve settings
dialogue, and it reads the add-on state of each Firefox profile. A profile
that holds the QtCurve theme add-on in a not active state gets no style
sheets, and earlier sheets leave.

With the setting off, the process deletes the files of the writer from each
Firefox profile. The process then stops, and no Firefox watch runs for that
user. To start it now, run:
systemctl --user start qtcurve-firefox-writer.service
EOF
}

_notice() {
	cat <<'EOF'
The QtCurve style dialogue writes GTK theme files into your home directory.
Before you remove the package, run qtcurve-gtk-writer --remove-gtk to delete
them. Run qtcurve-gtk-writer --remove-qt to delete your saved settings and
presets; the GTK theme then follows the defaults. Run qtcurve-gtk-writer
--purge-settings to delete both.

The Firefox writer of this package writes two style sheets into each Firefox
profile. Run qtcurve-firefox-writer --remove to delete those files. pacman
deletes no file under a home directory.
EOF
}

post_install() {
	_start_notice
	_notice
}

post_upgrade() {
	_start_notice
	_notice
}

pre_remove() {
	_notice
}
